---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={"A Minimal Browser UI That Stays Out of Your Way | Blanc"}
  description={"Blanc replaces a traditional tab strip and toolbar with one floating island for web search, tabs, navigation, direct site controls, and page actions."}
  path="/features/island"
  page="feature-island"
  current="features"
  ogDescription={"One floating island for web search, tabs, navigation, direct site controls, and page actions."}
  ogImage="/feature-island.png"
  ogImageAlt={"Blanc's floating island showing blancbrowser.com, tab dots, navigation, and the blocking control."}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://blancbrowser.com/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Features", "item": "https://blancbrowser.com/features" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "The Blanc island", "item": "https://blancbrowser.com/features/island" }
  ]
}
</script>

<main class="feature-page feature-detail-page">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/features">features</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">the island</span></nav>
  <section class="feature-hero feature-hero--detail" aria-labelledby="island-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">the blanc island</p>
    <h1 id="island-title">One small island. The whole browser.</h1>
    <p>Search, tabs, navigation, the current site, and page controls live together—so the page stays in front.</p>
  </section>
  <figure class="product-capture feature-capture">
    <div class="demo-stage island-figure" data-page-tone="github" role="img" aria-label="Blanc's floating island resting over the GitHub website, showing tab dots, back and forward navigation, and the current domain github.com.">
      <div class="demo-page" aria-hidden="true"><div class="bar w1"></div><div class="bar w2"></div><div class="bar w3"></div><div class="bar w4"></div></div>
      <picture>
        <source media="(max-width: 560px)" srcset="/shots/mobile/github.jpg">
        <img class="demo-shot show" src="/shots/desktop/github.jpg" loading="lazy" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
      </picture>
      <div class="demo-island" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="pill">
          <div class="pnav">
            <span class="pbtn"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M9.75 3.5 5.25 8l4.5 4.5"/></svg></span>
            <span class="pbtn off"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M6.25 3.5 10.75 8l-4.5 4.5"/></svg></span>
          </div>
          <div class="dots"><span></span><span class="cur"></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="pill-fav" style="background-image:url('/favicons/github.com.ico')"></span>
          <span class="domain">github.com</span>
          <span class="pill-shortcuts"><span class="pill-shortcut" title="New tab (⌘T)"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 3.25v9.5M3.25 8h9.5"/></svg></span></span>
          <span class="shield shield-quiet"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 1.8l5 1.9v3.8c0 3.1-2.1 5.3-5 6.7-2.9-1.4-5-3.6-5-6.7V3.7z"/><path d="M4.4 11.47 12.61 3.55"/></svg></span>
          <span class="psep"></span>
          <div class="pacts">
            <span class="pbtn"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M12.42 10.35a5 5 0 1 1-4.42-7.35c1.4 0 2.74.56 3.74 1.53L13 5.78"/><path d="M13 3v2.78h-2.78"/></svg></span>
            <span class="pbtn heart"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 13.25C4.6 11 2.75 8.9 2.75 6.6a2.85 2.85 0 0 1 5.25-1.54A2.85 2.85 0 0 1 13.25 6.6c0 2.3-1.85 4.4-5.25 6.65z"/></svg></span>
            <span class="pbtn"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M4.75 4.75l6.5 6.5M11.25 4.75l-6.5 6.5"/></svg></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>The island floats above the web page instead of reserving a permanent toolbar.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="room-title">
    <div><p class="section-kicker">the page gets the room</p><h2 id="room-title">The controls are close, not constantly present.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Keep the web in front.</h3><p>Blanc does not pin a traditional tab strip and toolbar above every page. The island leaves the web with more of its own room.</p></article>
      <article><h3>See the essentials at a glance.</h3><p>At rest, the island shows the tabs in your current group as dots, the site you are on, and a quiet shield. Click the shield to see the connection and change Blanc Blocker for that site.</p></article>
      <article><h3>It notices you coming.</h3><p>Move toward the island and it rises and grows a little, settling before you click and easing back as you leave. It follows how close you are rather than switching on at a threshold, so there is no edge to feel—and it stays completely still while another app has focus.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Opening it is a movement, not a cut.</h3><p>The command bar grows out of the resting island—starting at its exact size and shape, corners rounding out as it expands—and shrinks back into it when you dismiss. If you have reduce motion turned on, both of these are off entirely.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Search without leaving the island.</h3><p>Start typing and Blanc blends your open tabs, favorites, history, and groups with live suggestions from the search engine you chose in Settings. Press Enter to search exactly what you typed.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Open your whole session in one place.</h3><p>Open the island to switch tabs, navigate, favorite a page, start a private tab, or use the browser's commands—without moving the page underneath.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="island-personal-title">
    <div><p class="section-kicker">little everyday choices</p><h2 id="island-personal-title">Get to a new page with one click.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>A Plus that puts you straight into the address field.</h3><p>The resting Island’s Plus opens one regular, ungrouped tab and focuses its address field. It sits beside the slash-command keycap. In vertical-tabs mode, use the rail’s New tab control instead.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Choose the icon you want to keep in your Dock.</h3><p>On macOS, Settings offers Sunrise, Sunrise Dark, Paper, and Ink. All four app-icon choices are free; no Patron subscription is required.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Choose what a new tab looks like.</h3><p>Try a list of Favorites, local frequent sites, or a Mahjong board. <a href="/features/start-page" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="start-page" data-cta-position="related-feature">Explore the five Start Page layouts</a>.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-close" aria-labelledby="island-close-title"><p class="section-kicker">see less browser</p><h2 id="island-close-title">Leave the chrome behind. Keep the controls.</h2><a class="cta" href="/download" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="island" data-cta-position="feature-close">download blanc</a></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
